(Risk and Return, and Why Diversification Works) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Expected return always comes from accepting uncertainty. A product that) Tj
T*
(advertises high return with no risk usually hides the risk somewhere else,) Tj
T*
(often in liquidity or credit quality.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Before investing, answer three questions:) Tj
T*
(what is the underlying asset, where does the return come from,) Tj
T*
(and how much could be lost in the worst case.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Diversification reduces the impact of any single asset, sector or region.) Tj
T*
(Buying many funds with overlapping holdings is not real diversification.) Tj
T*
(Spreading across asset classes matters more than spreading within one class.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
