(Common Behavioral Biases in Investing) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Loss aversion: losses feel roughly twice as painful as equivalent gains,) Tj
T*
(which pushes people to sell good assets too early and hold bad ones too long.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Recency bias: assuming the last year's return predicts the next ten years.) Tj
T*
(Markets mean-revert far more than recent performance suggests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Herding: buying because others are buying, usually near the peak.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Overconfidence: trading more frequently and underperforming after costs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Anchoring: fixating on the purchase price instead of the current fundamentals.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A written investment policy, reviewed once a year, counters most of these.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
